  abstract = {NEW YORK TIMES~BESTSELLER {$\bullet$} WINNER OF THE PULITZER PRIZE {$\bullet$} One of the most acclaimed books of our time, this modern classic ``has set a new standard for reporting on poverty'' (Barbara Ehrenreich,~The New York Times Book Review).In~Evicted, Princeton sociologist and MacArthur ``Genius'' Matthew Desmond follows eight families in Milwaukee as they each struggle to keep a roof over their heads. Hailed as ``wrenching and revelatory'' (The Nation), ``vivid and unsettling'' (New York Review of Books),~Evicted~transforms our understanding of poverty and economic exploitation while providing fresh ideas for solving one of twenty-first-century America's most devastating problems. Its unforgettable scenes of hope and loss remind us of the centrality of home, without which nothing else is possible.~NAMED ONE OF THE BEST BOOKS OF THE YEAR BY President Barack Obama {$\bullet~$}The New York Times Book Review~{$\bullet~$}The Boston Globe~{$\bullet~$}The Washington Post~{$\bullet~$}NPR~{$\bullet$} Entertainment Weekly~{$\bullet~$}The New Yorker {$\bullet~$}Bloomberg~{$\bullet~$}Esquire~{$\bullet$} BuzzFeed {$\bullet$} Fortune~{$\bullet~$}San Francisco Chronicle {$\bullet~$}Milwaukee Journal Sentinel~{$\bullet~$}St. Louis Post-Dispatch~{$\bullet~$}Politico~{$\bullet~$}The Week~{$\bullet~$}Chicago Public Library~{$\bullet~$}BookPage~{$\bullet~$}Kirkus Reviews~{$\bullet~$}Library Journal~{$\bullet~$} Publishers Weekly~{$\bullet$} Booklist {$\bullet~$}Shelf AwarenessWINNER OF:~The National Book Critics Circle Award for Nonfiction {$\bullet$} The PEN/John Kenneth Galbraith Award for Nonfiction {$\bullet$} The Andrew Carnegie Medal for Excellence in Nonfiction {$\bullet$} The Hillman Prize for Book Journalism {$\bullet$} The PEN/New England Award {$\bullet$} The~Chicago Tribune~Heartland PrizeFINALIST FOR THE~LOS ANGELES TIMES~BOOK PRIZE AND THE KIRKUS PRIZE``Evicted~stands among the very best of the social justice books.''---Ann Patchett, author of~Bel 