``language of democracy and liberation.'' (Postone, 2006, p. 104)
\par
``the sort of future society and polity implicitly expressed by the political praxis of militant social movements that distinguish military from civilian targets differs from that implied by the praxis of movements that make no such distinction'' (Postone, 2006, p. 105)
